s must be enabled on a field by field basis.'=>'Show all fields in REST API. If unchecked fields must be enabled on a field by field basis.','Add REST API support for this Pod.'=>'Add REST API support for this Pod.','REST API'=>'REST API','https://pods.io/about/'=>'https://pods.io/about/','Pods Framework Team'=>'Pods Framework Team','Pods is a framework for creating, managing, and deploying customized content types and fields'=>'Pods is a framework for creating, managing, and deploying customised content types and fields','https://pods.io/'=>'https://pods.io/','Pods - Custom Content Types and Fields'=>'Pods - Custom Content Types and Fields','Allowed Files'=>'Allowed Files','Current Color'=>'Current Color','Select Color'=>'Select Colour','Default'=>'Default','After Content'=>'After Content','Before Content'=>'Before Content','You must specify a Pods Template or create a custom template, using <a href="https://docs.pods.io/displaying-pods/magic-tags/using-magic-tags/" title="Using Magic Tags" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">magic tags</a>.'=>'You must specify a Pods Template or create a custom template, using <a href="https://docs.pods.io/displaying-pods/magic-tags/using-magic-tags/" title="Using Magic Tags" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">magic tags</a>.','Upgrade Complete!'=>'Upgrade Complete!','Optimizing Your Relationships'=>'Optimising Your Relationships','During this process your Relationships will be optimized.'=>'During this process your Relationships will be optimised.','Preparing Your Relationships for Upgrade'=>'Preparing Your Relationships for Upgrade','We will prepare your relationships for the upgrade. If any issues are found they will be displayed below for your review. Be sure to backup your database before continuing onto the next step for the Upgrade.'=>'We will prepare your relationships for the upgrade. If any issues are found they will be displayed below for your review. Be sure to backup your database before continuing onto the next step for the Upgrade.','We need to run a few updates to your database to optimize your relationship data.'=>'We need to run a few updates to your database to optimize your relationship data.','Thanks for upgrading your Pods 2.x site! We sincerely hope you enjoy over two years worth of planning and work, available to you for <em>free</em>.'=>'Thanks for upgrading your Pods 2.x site! We sincerely hope you enjoy over two years worth of planning and work, available to you for <em>free</em>.','Migration Complete!'=>'Migration Complete!','Start using Pods'=>'Start using Pods','Cleanup'=>'Cleanup','1.x Updates'=>'1.x Updates','Migrating Your Content'=>'Migrating Your Content','During this process your Pods, Settings, and Content will be migrated into the optimized Pods 2.x architecture. We will not delete any of your old data, the tables will remain until you choose to clean them up after a successful upgrade.'=>'During this process your Pods, Settings, and Content will be migrated into the optimised Pods 2.x architecture. We will not delete any of your old data, the tables will remain until you choose to clean them up after a successful upgrade.','Content'=>'Content','Helpers'=>'Helpers','Pod Pages'=>'Pod Pages','Templates'=>'Templates','Item Indexes'=>'Item Indexes','Relationships'=>'Relationships','Preparing Your Content for Migration'=>'Preparing Your Content for Migration','We will prepare all of your Pods, Settings, and Content for migration. If any issues are found they will be displayed below for your review. Be sure to backup your database before continuing onto the next step for Migration.'=>'We will prepare all of your Pods, Settings, and Content for migration. If any issues are found they will be displayed below for your review. Be sure to backup your database before continuing onto the next step for Migration.','Due to a number of optimizations in Pods 2.x, we need to run a few updates to your database. This should not remove or change your existing Pod data from 1.x, so if you wish to rollback to Pods 1.x - you can easily do that.'=>'Due to a number of optimizations in Pods 2.x, we need to run a few updates to your database. This should not remove or change your existing Pod data from 1.x, so if you wish to rollback to Pods 1.x - you can easily do that.','Welcome to Pods 2.x! We sincerely hope you enjoy over two years worth of planning and work, available to you for <em>free</em>.'=>'Welcome to Pods 2.x! We sincerely hope you enjoy over two years worth of planning and work, available to you for <em>free</em>.','Prepare'=>'Prepare','Getting Started'=>'Getting Started','Upgrade Pods'=>'Upgrade Pods','A service that provides realtime continuous backups, restores, and security scanning.'=>'A service that provides realtime continuous backups, restores, and security scanning.','Click to sign up'=>'Click to sign up','1 free month'=>'1 free month','The all-in-one WordPress backup plugin to easily backup, restore, and migrate to any number of local or external locations.'=>'The all-in-one WordPress backup plugin to easily backup, restore, and migrate to any number of local or external locations.','Coupon Code'=>'Coupon Code','Receive 25% off'=>'Receive 25% off','We recommend that you back your database up, it can really save you in a bind or a really weird situation that you may not be expecting. Check out a few options we think are <em>great</em> below.'=>'We recommend that you back your database up, it can really save you in a bind or a really weird situation that you may not be expecting. Check out a few options we think are <em>great</em> below.','Insert'=>'Insert','ID or Slug'=>'ID or Slug','Pods Page'=>'Pods Page','Choose a Pod'=>'Choose a Pod','Embed content from a Pods Page'=>'Embed content from a Pods Page','Display a field from this item'=>'Display a field from this item','Display a field from a single Pod item'=>'Display a field from a single Pod item','List multiple Pod items'=>'List multiple Pod items','What would you like to do?'=>'What would you like to do?','Pods &raquo; Embed'=>'Pods &raquo; Embed','No Hierarchical Fields found'=>'No Hierarchical Fields found','If you delete the "name" field, we need to specify the field to use as your primary title field. This field will serve as an index of your content. Most commonly this field represents the name of a person, place, thing, or a summary field.'=>'If you delete the "name" field, we need to specify the field to use as your primary title field. This field will serve as an index of your content. Most commonly this field represents the name of a person, place, thing, or a summary field.','Title Field'=>'Title Field','Detail Page URL'=>'Detail Page URL','Function to call when updating counts'=>'Function to call when updating counts','Remember order saved on Post Types'=>'Remember order saved on Post Types','Custom Query Var Name'=>'Custom Query Var Name','Hierarchical Permalinks'=>'Hierarchical Permalinks','Comma-separated list of custom "supports" values to pass to register_post_type.'=>'Comma-separated list of custom "supports" values to pass to register_post_type.','Advanced Supports'=>'Advanced Supports','Jetpack Markdown Support'=>'Jetpack Markdown Support','Jetpack Publicize Support'=>'Jetpack Publicize Support','YARPP Support'=>'YARPP Support','Genesis: Simple Sidebars'=>'Genesis: Simple Sidebars','Genesis: Layouts'=>'Genesis: Layouts','Genesis: SEO'=>'Genesis: SEO','Page Attributes'=>'Page Attributes','Revisions'=>'Revisions','Trackbacks'=>'Trackbacks','Excerpt'=>'Excerpt','Featured Image'=>'Featured Image','Author'=>'Author','Title'=>'Title','Supports'=>'Supports','Not Found in Trash'=>'Not Found in Trash','Not Found'=>'Not Found','No Related Fields Found'=>'No Related Fields Found','-- Select Table --'=>'-- Select Table --','Other'=>'Other','Unique'=>'Unique','Required'=>'Required','Options'=>'Options','Bi-directional fields will update their related field for any item you select. This feature is only available for two relationships between two Pods.<br /><br />For example, when you update a Parent pod item to relate to a Child item, when you go to edit that Child item you will see the Parent pod item selected.'=>'Bi-directional fields will update their related field for any item you select. This feature is only available for two relationships between two Pods.<br /><br />For example, when you update a Parent pod item to relate to a Child item, when you go to edit that Child item you will see the Parent pod item selected.','Bi-directional Field'=>'Bi-directional Field','Related Table'=>'Related Table','One option per line, use <em>value|Label</em> for separate values and labels'=>'One option per line, use <em>value|Label</em> for separate values and labels','Custom Defined Options'=>'Custom Defined Options','Field Type'=>'Field Type','<h3>Taxonomies</h3> A taxonomy is a way to group Post Types.'=>'<h3>Taxonomies</h3> A taxonomy is a way to group Post Types.','Taxonomy'=>'Taxonomy','<h3>Post Types</h3> WordPress can hold and display many different types of content. Internally, these are all stored in the same place, in the wp_posts table. These are differentiated by a column called post_type.'=>'<h3>Post Types</h3> WordPress can hold and display many different types of content. Internally, these are all stored in the same place, in the wp_posts table. These are differentiated by a column called post_type.','Post Type'=>'Post Type','Post Types (Posts, Pages, etc..)'=>'Post Types (Posts, Pages, etc..)','Extend an Existing Content Type'=>'Extend an Existing Content Type','Extending an existing Content Type allows you to add fields to it and take advantage of the Pods architecture for management and optionally for theming.'=>'Extending an existing Content Type allows you to add fields to it and take advantage of the Pods architecture for management and optionally for theming.','Table Based'=>'Table Based','Meta Based (WP Default)'=>'Meta Based (WP Default)','<h3>Storage Types</h3> Table based storage will operate in a way where each field you create for your content type becomes a field in a table. Meta based storage relies upon the WordPress meta storage table for all field data.'=>'<h3>Storage Types</h3> Table based storage will operate in a way where each field you create for your content type becomes a field in a table. Meta based storage relies upon the WordPress meta storage table for all field data.','<h3>Pod Identifier</h3> This is different than the labels users will see in the WordPress admin areas, it is the name you will use to programatically reference this object throughout your theme, WordPress, and other PHP.'=>'<h3>Pod Identifier</h3> This is different than the labels users will see in the WordPress admin areas, it is the name you will use to programatically reference this object throughout your theme, WordPress, and other PHP.','Pod Name'=>'Pod Name','<h3>Menu Location</h3> This is the location where the new settings page will be added in the WordPress Dashboard menu.'=>'<h3>Menu Location</h3> This is the location where the new settings page will be added in the WordPress Dashboard menu.','<h3>Menu Label</h3> This is the label that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for your settings.'=>'<h3>Menu Label</h3> This is the label that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for your settings.','Menu Label'=>'Menu Label','<h3>Page Title</h3> This is the text that will appear at the top of your settings page.'=>'<h3>Page Title</h3> This is the text that will appear at the top of your settings page.','<h3>Plural Label</h3> This is the label for more than 1 item (Plural) that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for managing the content.'=>'<h3>Plural Label</h3> This is the label for more than 1 item (Plural) that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for managing the content.','Plural Label'=>'Plural Label','<h3>Singular Label</h3> This is the label for 1 item (Singular) that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for managing the content.'=>'<h3>Singular Label</h3> This is the label for 1 item (Singular) that will appear throughout the WordPress admin area for managing the content.','Singular Label'=>'Singular Label','Custom Taxonomy (like Categories or Tags)'=>'Custom Taxonomy (like Categories or Tags)','Custom Post Type (like Posts or Pages)'=>'Custom Post Type (like Posts or Pages)','<h3>Content Types</h3> There are many content types to choose from, we have put together a comparison between them all to help you decide what fits your needs best.'=>'<h3>Content Types</h3> There are many content types to choose from, we have put together a comparison between them all to help you decide what fits your needs best.','Content Type'=>'Content Type','Create a New Content Type'=>'Create a New Content Type','Creating a new Content Type allows you to control exactly what that content type does, how it acts like, the fields it has, and the way you manage it.'=>'Creating a new Content Type allows you to control exactly what that content type does, how it acts like, the fields it has, and the way you manage it.','Extend any existing content type within WordPress, including <strong>Post Types</strong> (Posts, Pages, etc), <strong>Taxonomies</strong> (Categories, Tags, etc), <strong>Media</strong>, <strong>Users</strong>, or <strong>Comments</strong>.'=>'Extend any existing content type within WordPress, including <strong>Post Types</strong> (Posts, Pages, etc), <strong>Taxonomies</strong> (Categories, Tags, etc), <strong>Media</strong>, <strong>Users</strong>, or <strong>Comments</strong>.','Extend Existing'=>'Extend Existing','Create entirely new content types using <strong>Post Types</strong>, <strong>Taxonomies</strong>, or <strong>Custom Settings Pages</strong>.'=>'Create entirely new content types using <strong>Post Types</strong>, <strong>Taxonomies</strong>, or <strong>Custom Settings Pages</strong>.','Create New'=>'Create New','Not sure what content type you should use? Check out our <a href="https://docs.pods.io/creating-editing-pods/compare-content-types/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Content Type Comparison</a> to help you decide.'=>'Not sure what content type you should use? Check out our <a href="https://docs.pods.io/creating-editing-pods/compare-content-types/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Content Type Comparison</a> to help you decide.','Pods are content types that you can customize and define fields for based on your needs. You can choose to create a Custom Post Type, Custom Taxonomy, or Custom Settings Pages for site-specific data. You can also extend existing content types like WP Objects such as Post Types, Taxonomies, Users, or Comments.'=>'Pods are content types that you can customise and define fields for based on your needs. You can choose to create a Custom Post Type, Custom Taxonomy, or Custom Settings Pages for site-specific data. You can also extend existing content types like WP Objects such as Post Types, Taxonomies, Users, or Comments.','Configure'=>'Configure','Create or Extend'=>'Create or Extend','Back to Manage'=>'Back to Manage','Add New Pod'=>'Add New Pod','Cleanup &amp; Reset'=>'Cleanup &amp; Reset','Clear Pods Cache'=>'Clear Pods Cache','Are you sure you want to Reset your Weekend?

There is no going back, you cannot reclaim anything you\'ve gained throughout your weekend.

You are about to be groundhoggin\' it'=>'Are you sure you want to Reset your Weekend?

There is no going back, you cannot reclaim anything you\'ve gained throughout your weekend.

You are about to be groundhoggin\' it','By resetting the weekend, you will be sent back to Friday night and the weekend you\'ve just spent will be erased. You will retain all of your memories of the weekend, and be able to relive it in any way you wish.'=>'By resetting the weekend, you will be sent back to Friday night and the weekend you\'ve just spent will be erased. You will retain all of your memories of the weekend, and be able to relive it in any way you wish.','This feature has been exclusively built for Pods to help developers suffering from "Monday", and allows them to reset the weekend.'=>'This feature has been exclusively built for Pods to help developers suffering from "Monday", and allows them to reset the weekend.','Reset Weekend'=>'Reset Weekend','Deactivate and Delete Pods data'=>'Deactivate and Delete Pods data','Reset Pods settings and data'=>'Reset Pods settings and data','<strong>Please Note:</strong> This does not remove any items from any Post Types, Taxonomies, Media, Users, or Comments data you have added/modified.'=>'<strong>Please Note:</strong> This does not remove any items from any Post Types, Taxonomies, Media, Users, or Comments data you have added/modified.','This will delete Pods 2.x settings, data, and deactivate itself once done. Your database will be as if Pods 2.x never existed.'=>'This will delete Pods 2.x settings, data, and deactivate itself once done. Your database will be as if Pods 2.x never existed.','Deactivate and Delete Pods 2.x data'=>'Deactivate and Delete Pods 2.x data','Reset Pods 2.x settings and data'=>'Reset Pods 2.x settings and data','Are you sure you want to do this?

This is a good time to make sure you have a backup. We are deleting all of the data that surrounds 2.x, resetting it to a clean first install.'=>'Are you sure you want to do this?

This is a good time to make sure you have a backup. We are deleting all of the data that surrounds 2.x, resetting it to a clean first install.','This does not remove any items from any Post Types, Taxonomies, Media, Users, or Comments data you have added/modified. Any custom fields stored using the table storage component, content in Advanced Content Types, and relationships between posts will be lost.'=>'This does not remove any items from any Post Types, Taxonomies, Media, Users, or Comments data you have added/modified. Any custom fields stored using the table storage component, content in Advanced Content Types, and relationships between posts will be lost.','This does not delete any Pods 1.x data, it simply resets the Pods 2.x settings, removes all of it\'s data, and performs a fresh install.'=>'This does not delete any Pods 1.x data, it simply resets the Pods 2.x settings, removes all of its data, and performs a fresh install.','Reset Pods 2.x'=>'Reset Pods 2.x','Delete Pods 1.x settings and data'=>'Delete Pods 1.x settings and data','This will delete all of your Pods 1.x data, it\'s only recommended if you\'ve verified your data has been properly migrated into Pods 2.x.'=>'This will delete all of your Pods 1.x data, it\'s only recommended if you\'ve verified your data has been properly migrated into Pods 2.x.','Delete Pods 1.x data'=>'Delete Pods 1.x data','Please Note:'=>'Please Note:','To report <strong>bugs or request features</strong>, go to our <a href="https://github.com/pods-framework/pods/issues?sort=updated&direction=desc&state=open" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.'=>'To report <strong>bugs or request features</strong>, go to our <a href="https://github.com/pods-framework/pods/issues?sort=updated&direction=desc&state=open" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.','There are many resources available to help you learn to use Pods <a href="https://pods.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">on our website</a>'